<title>USA: Salomon issues $400 million CPI-linked debt.</title>
<headline>Salomon issues $400 million CPI-linked debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue of inflation-indexed securities from Salomon Inc was priced on Friday, according to lead manager Salomon Brothers.</p>
<p>BORROWER SALOMON INC</p>
<p>AMT $400	     COUPON 3.65 PCT   MATURITY 2/14/2002</p>
<p>TYPE CPI-LINKED    ISS PRICE 99.04   FIRST PAY DATE 8/14/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S Baa1  YIELD 3.88 PCT    PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BBB	 SPREAD 65 BP	CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>NOTES: Priced over U.S. Treasury TIPS.</p>
<p>U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1672</p>
</text>
